+# Source continuous coffee cell (B06)
+
+`MJ-CELL-BV01` uses `engineering-mujoco-cell-v1`: one `single_world` MuJoCo3.17.0 worker, one model, a20ms Source tick and10×2ms physics substeps. This is modeled software evidence (`accepted:false`, `not_calibrated`). It does not close native-controller, calibration, commissioning or hardware gates.
+
+The normal portable bootstrap supplies the shared-world factory after verified MuJoCo configuration. Composition readiness checks the exact project, cell fixture closure, lock, worker identity, controller policy and clock, disk capacity and exclusive engine slot, then creates the actual model with all cup slots inactive. It caches only a successful exact identity and rechecks mutable prerequisites and capacity. Abort/failure never caches success; ownership lasts through actual process close. A run's own readiness requires a live verified world identity; readiness cannot recover an unknown physical run.
+
+The new `coffee-delivery-cell-v1` fixture copies all B05 physical/model/program/load/project/handoff files byte for byte. Its new scene admits a signed navigation extent `[-0.6,-0.6]..[6,4]` on the existing open floor, with the complete hull and swept-turn checks. `grid-diff-world-v4` applies0.004m to **every translation**,0.008m terminal position and0.016rad terminal yaw. The v2 design braking bound is0.25m/s² (assumed controller design, not a measured hardware guarantee), while command acceleration remains0.5m/s². Every translation remains active until actual speed is at most the existing0.01m/s stopped threshold; within its position tolerance the desired linear command is zero and the existing ramp brakes it. Legacy routes/options retain their original bounds and tolerances. The manifest exposes `worldExtent` for downstream viewport and replay admission. B05's local handoff rig proves neither this route nor Source custody.
+
+Source first consumes the assigned robot's actual load-stop arrival, then requires10 consecutive measured dock ticks (XY≤0.01m, yaw≤0.02rad, speed≤0.01m/s, angular speed≤0.02rad/s). The arm remains a real arm snapshot. Explicit `CoffeePlantPorts.custodyEvidence:'correlated'` requires CupLedger and disables synthesized receiver completion; absent mode retains legacy behavior. Motion is interlocked while any arm program runs, while the arm holds a cup or after a latched stop. Observation and cancellation processing continues through that interlock.
+
+`mujoco_world_arm` and `mujoco_world_tray` are distinct logical observers, both `fidelity:'modeled'`, sharing engine/boot/scene/clock/tick/substep provenance. Grasp requires actual gripper hold plus observed lift. Release and receiver support are independently evaluated from the **current committed snapshot**: open/not held versus actual support contact, polygon margin and relative motion sustained for25 consecutive ticks. Same-snapshot pairing preserves the existing500000000ns coordinator receipt-age bound; a pause expires receipts rather than retimestamping cached booleans. Distinct observer IDs alone never prove a transfer.
+
+The Source pending transfer and journal bind cup/command/transfer/payload hash/control epoch/recipient. Free cup IDs remain stable through nozzle→arm→tray→recipient. Placements only activate the nozzle cup or remove it after a real `CupHandedOff`; each binds its `CupBound`/`CupHandedOff` journal event. Transfers never teleport, weld or replace a cup. Reports distinguish last-confirmed Source ownership from physical known/lost/unknown state.
+
+Optional `worldControl` is Source command provenance, not a custody receipt or caller-supplied collision permission. It records selected program/stage/waypoint, Source transfer event and identity, attachment proxy, interlock and stop. Old providers reject it. `world-full-capsule-v1` independently reads consecutive actual joints against complete current AMR geometry and admitted program/phase/pair/region rules. Geometry and all-substep native contact checks remain separate. Legacy ARM03 retains its4096-interval checkpoint cap and honest truncation result.
+
+Full-world review uses the existing30,000-tick,256KiB/row,400MiB inflated observation limits and100MiB durable directory quota. Its additional trusted Source-journal input is bounded to10,000 entries and16MiB. Missing context, invalid identities, journal mismatch, gaps, quota exhaustion and uncertainty yield incomplete/not_run/fail; there is no silent truncation or success fallback. The review accepts the trusted Source session journal, not a browser-provided event string.
+
+Source hot state uses the explicitly reported `world_durable_v1` policy:16 recent derived collision intervals/referenced worlds and joint/prop/debug samples. Current actual state, command/generator/program/grip state, counters, cumulative tracking statistics and immutable first-failure geometry remain intact. Every live sweep still runs and every raw world observation remains durable. Legacy providers keep their4096 cap. The world legacy ARM03 result remains derived from its bounded cache and never becomes a pass merely because a full trace is reconstructed.
+
+Normal runtime reports capture the public horizon, manifest, critical state, Source journal/effects and view under the run's action boundary. The recorder separately captures immutable published refs and a bounded durable tail in its own serial boundary, without flushing, finishing or republishing. Reconstruction happens outside the action boundary and never writes full history back into checkpoint/preview state. World joint/prop trace files use content hashes, so another report cannot overwrite an older report's references. `world-committed-trace-v1` explicitly includes all committed world ticks, including the priming snapshot and idle/stopped ticks; tracking statistics separately cover active program ticks.
+
+Normal `worldSweep` exposes the named complete interval method at a captured Source horizon. `scope.prefixCovered`, `scope.streamFinalized` and business `outcome.status`/`served` are separate axes: a gap-free closed40-tick stream can be finalized with served0. Active or terminal prefixes never imply a finalized recording or successful mission. Captured uncommitted ACKH+1 is excluded from Source-H reports. Missing/corrupt/oversize/ambiguous publication history yields explicit unavailable/not_run; there is no deduplication or repair. Read-only reopen uses the retained admitted bundle and horizon, never the installed latest fixture or a replacement engine.
+
+World stop events use the actual observed snapshot tick via a Source-only override, without advancing generator time or claiming that physical motion stopped early. Native disturbance, measured violation, public latch and next physical command remain distinct timeline facts.
+
+Registered server-only development disturbances are `world-dock-drift-v1` (2000N mapX,10 substeps, actual closed-gripper pre-release) and `world-cup-fall-v1` ([30,0,30]N map,10 substeps, actual supported transport). Each is admitted once at world creation, consumed before effect, cleared in `finally` and recorded with native request identity, fixed force/frame and before/after observations. Nominal worlds admit neither. These are deliberate disturbances, not claims of natural slip. A lost ACK remains unknown without retry; read-only reopen cannot birth another cup or respawn the world.
+
+Campaign definition: `robotics/simulation-mujoco/campaigns/mj-cell-bv01-v1.json`. Exact loaded identities, retained development failures, nominal/fault outcomes and commands are recorded in the B06 task report and accompanying evidence. Normal-bootstrap smoke and campaign entry are separate evidence scopes.
+
+Development measurements after bounding the caches: the same closed checkpoint shrank from11,942,457 to187,704bytes with its critical projection unchanged; median stringify41.742→0.624ms, cloneCoffee52.119→0.422ms and cloneArm47.078→0.401ms. These are CPU diagnostics, excluding filesystem durability and native execution. A real Source2200-tick/44s prefix took75.172s stepping (0.585×), max checkpoint156,378bytes; its full2200-interval geometry and native-contact readback passed. This is not a complete nominal campaign or a browser1× pacing claim. Worker/IPC timing was not measured; B07b owns the production browser/pause/IPC gate.
+
+World controller v3 adds an assumed0.20m terminal approach behind the unchanged goal in its yaw frame. This is an internal waypoint within the same Source command, with full footprint/swept-leg validation and no unchecked fallback. A final feedback-driven translation follows the large staging turn. The observed v2 return ended2.151mm from goal before turning, then shifted8.908mm during the final turn and settled10.473mm away; that failed seed remains development evidence. The isolated regression uses the exact retained XY displacement during a >2rad near-goal turn under the same stated lag for both policies. A broader6mm turn-offset model still exposes earlier small-leg robustness limits; no general convergence or calibrated-dynamics claim follows from the isolated test.
+
+World v4 supersedes the unsafe forward candidate with an explicit reverse terminal approach: stage at goalXY+0.20*[cos(goalYaw),sin(goalYaw)], orient to goalYaw, then feedback-drive negative velocity to the same Source goal. Its body heading is travel heading pluspi; stopping footprints keep the full asymmetric body orientation. Rear invalid/stale/missing/partial data and dynamic rear points block motion, including the first tick after a settled rotation retires. Signed acceleration and wheel bounds and actual pose/both-speed arrival hold remain unchanged. Old v1/v2/v3 scene metadata remains readable, while the live cell fixture/readiness admits v4.
+
+The failed v3 native route hit chassis/base/c0 against the low nozzle stand at4467; no geometric clearance pass is inferred from the arm oracle. Its20cm forward staging pose itself overlaps the stand. The v4 scoped return replay retains exact command-prefix SHA00939c6c98164d137f46855f93e9631a7c874b68eb793b6aff42939c0aa8fb71 and reproduces only the measured arm-joint/AMRdrive-pose subset exactly, then passes2131separate arm sweeps and all native contacts. Final error0.444mm, yawerror0.014807rad,12strict dock samples. This is diagnostic evidence, not new Source custody or business qualification.
+
+V4 terminal arrival also retains the original goal while requesting bounded zero through the previous-sent-command ramp. Source receives arrived only when both sent velocities are zero and the actual pose/both-speed hold is still satisfied; the actual window, rear sensing, no-progress and deadline are rechecked every tick. No sticky arrival latch is introduced. The first scoped v4 probe establishes clearance/convergence but retained an old terminal-zero angular-ramp exception; the subsequent scoped probe verifies the corrected command bounds. Legacy/v1-v3 terminal behavior is unchanged.
