@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+# Continuous Source coffee cell
+
+Software-only development fixture, `accepted:false`, `not_calibrated`. Derived from the independently reviewed B05 `coffee-delivery-world-v1`. All arm/mobile model, gripper, contact, program and load files retain the reviewed bytes; this fixture adds Source workflow/control evidence and an explicit world navigation policy.
+
+The physical cell remains at its reviewed coordinates. The planner uses a declared signed open-floor apron `[-0.6,-0.6]..[6,4]` with the complete AMR footprint, consistent with the existing plane and absence of walls. Controller `grid-diff-world-v4` declares design braking deceleration0.25m/s² under the unchanged0.5m/s² command ramp bound. Every translation stays active through actual stopped-speed settling; desired linear motion becomes zero inside the leg tolerance. This is assumed control design, not a physical braking certificate. The world-only translation tolerance is0.004m for every translation, terminal position0.008m/yaw0.016rad; all legacy providers retain their previous policies. Dock readiness remains10 ticks at0.01m/0.02rad; tray receipt remains25 consecutive ticks with actual support, polygon margin and relative motion. Arrival is consumed before Source permits picking; motion remains interlocked through withdrawal.
+
+Each `worldControl` is Source-owned command provenance bound to the actual `CupTransferRequested` journal entry, command/hash/epoch/program/stage. It supplies no caller-defined allowed contact pairs. Birth and recipient removal bind real `CupBound`/`CupHandedOff` events; custody transfer is never a placement. Arm/tray receipts are independent logical evaluations of the same engine observations, labeled modeled with shared boot/scene/tick provenance.
+
+The named `world-full-capsule-v1` review reads the complete bounded world stream and trusted Source journal, using consecutive actual joints and current full AMR geometry. It reports geometry and native substep contacts separately. Legacy ARM03 retains its4096-interval truncation result. Neither geometric review nor software custody evidence establishes native-controller, hardware, calibration or deployment readiness.
+
+Registered disturbances are server-only one-shot campaign presets: `world-dock-drift-v1` applies2000N along mapX for10×2ms substeps before release; `world-cup-fall-v1` applies[30,0,30]N in map for10 substeps during supported transport. Forces clear in `finally`; before/after observations and request identity are recorded. These are deliberate disturbances, not natural-slip results. Nominal worlds admit no disturbance.
+
+Source hot state declares `world_durable_v1`:16 recent derived samples/worlds, preserving critical control state, all sweep/stat counters and first-failure geometry. Raw world observations remain complete and durable. Normal reports capture the Source public horizon/journal and immutable stream refs/tail, then reconstruct transient full traces and `world-full-capsule-v1` coverage. `prefixCovered`, `streamFinalized` and business outcome are separate. Legacy ARM03 remains a bounded-cache result; read-only reopen uses this retained bundle, never a replacement world or latest fixture.
+
+World controller v4 uses the assumed `terminalApproachDistanceM=0.20` and `terminalApproachDirection=reverse`: the internal approach point is goal XY plus0.20m along goal yaw. It turns to goal yaw there and follows a negative-velocity terminal translation to the unchanged Source target, with lateral feedback. Already near-goal poses retain their previous behavior. Staging poses and terminal swept corridors retain the full asymmetric body footprint and signed bounds; an impossible corridor is refused. Rear motion requires fresh usable360-beam data. Travel direction and body yaw are distinct in rear stopping/invalid-beam checks and swept-turn checks. Planar LiDAR is not claimed to detect the low stand.
+
+The v3 forward staging candidate collided with the unchanged nozzle stand and is retained as failed evidence. The scoped v4 return diagnostic passed actual native contacts and separate arm sweeps, reaching0.444mm position error with12actual dock-window samples. This diagnostic is not Source nominal qualification. Native3-seed/fault campaigns remain the acceptance gate. No physical/program bytes, tolerances or legacy policy changed.
+
+V4 arrival keeps the goal active while the previous-sent-command ramp reaches exact zero. The actual window and sensor/progress/deadline guards remain active until the single Source arrival event. The first scoped v4 probe retained the old immediate-terminal-zero ramp exception; a separate corrected probe verifies that bound.
